Certificate stats: do not cache a result that has no remote certificate yet.

RTCStatsCollector::PrepareTransportCertificateStats_n() caches the per-
transport certificate pair on the first getStats() and returns that cache
until ClearCachedStatsReport() runs. ClearCachedStatsReport() is called on
SDP, ICE candidate and data-channel changes only, never when a DTLS
handshake completes. A getStats() issued between ICE connected and the end
of the DTLS handshake therefore stored a pair whose `remote` was empty, and
every later report kept omitting the remote certificate:
transport.remoteCertificateId stayed absent for the rest of the call.

The DTLS server (the answerer, a=setup:passive) is the side that hits it:
it only learns the client's certificate from the client's last flight, so
the window is wide. The transcript-v5 check (b) in the apps (DTLSFP 3.6)
polls getStats() for the negotiated certificates and fails closed after
5 s without a verdict. Observed 2026-10-01 on M150 a256-dplc-9: every
incoming call on Android ended 5 s after answer
("dtls_fp mismatch stage=stats", [dtls-diag] remoteCert=NONE
dtlsRole=server for the whole call), and some iOS-to-iOS calls ended the
same way (hsfatal r=1) depending on timing.

Fix: cache the result only when every transport reports a remote
certificate. Until then it is recomputed on each call (what the code did
before the cache existed). Once complete, behaviour is byte-for-byte
upstream: the existing CertificateStatsCache test still holds. New test
RTCStatsCollectorTest.CertificateStatsCacheWaitsForRemoteCertificate
(T10, peerconnection_unittests) reproduces the field failure.

Applies identically to every variant; nothing here depends on
rtc_qaudion_transport_strict.

diff --git a/pc/rtc_stats_collector.cc b/pc/rtc_stats_collector.cc
index 90cc23b..8b1afa1 100644
--- a/pc/rtc_stats_collector.cc
+++ b/pc/rtc_stats_collector.cc
@@ -2267,10 +2267,29 @@ RTCStatsCollector::PrepareTransportCertificateStats_n(
       transport_cert_stats.insert(
           std::make_pair(transport_name, std::move(certificate_stats_pair)));
     }
-    // Copy the result into the certificate cache for future reference.
+    // Q-Audion (P9): cache the result only once every transport reports the
+    // remote certificate. Nothing invalidates this cache when a DTLS
+    // handshake completes (ClearCachedStatsReport() runs on SDP, candidate
+    // and data-channel changes only), so a getStats() issued while DTLS was
+    // still in progress used to pin an entry without `remote` for the rest
+    // of the call: transport.remoteCertificateId stayed absent forever. The
+    // DTLS server side is the one that hits it, since it receives the
+    // client's certificate in the client's last flight. Until the result is
+    // complete it is recomputed on every call, which is what the code did
+    // before the cache existed.
+    bool qaudion_remote_complete = true;
     for (const auto& pair : transport_cert_stats) {
-      cached_certificates_by_transport_.insert(
-          std::make_pair(pair.first, pair.second.Copy()));
+      if (!pair.second.remote) {
+        qaudion_remote_complete = false;
+        break;
+      }
+    }
+    // Copy the result into the certificate cache for future reference.
+    if (qaudion_remote_complete) {
+      for (const auto& pair : transport_cert_stats) {
+        cached_certificates_by_transport_.insert(
+            std::make_pair(pair.first, pair.second.Copy()));
+      }
     }
   }
   return transport_cert_stats;
diff --git a/pc/rtc_stats_collector_unittest.cc b/pc/rtc_stats_collector_unittest.cc
index 75ec9c8..41f718a 100644
--- a/pc/rtc_stats_collector_unittest.cc
+++ b/pc/rtc_stats_collector_unittest.cc
@@ -1617,6 +1617,62 @@ TEST_P(RTCStatsCollectorTest, CertificateStatsCache) {
       third_report, updated_remote_certinfo->fingerprints[1]));
 }
 
+// Q-Audion (P9): a stats report taken while DTLS is still in progress (no
+// remote certificate yet) must not pin that incomplete result in the
+// certificate cache. Once the remote certificate is known it has to show up,
+// and from then on the cache behaves as upstream (see CertificateStatsCache).
+TEST_P(RTCStatsCollectorTest, CertificateStatsCacheWaitsForRemoteCertificate) {
+  const char kTransportName[] = "transport";
+
+  RTC_ALLOW_PLAN_B_DEPRECATION_BEGIN();
+  pc_->AddVoiceChannel("audio", kTransportName);
+  RTC_ALLOW_PLAN_B_DEPRECATION_END();
+
+  // Local certificate only: the DTLS handshake has not delivered the peer's
+  // certificate yet.
+  std::unique_ptr<CertificateInfo> local_certinfo =
+      CreateFakeCertificateAndInfoFromDers({"LocalCertA"});
+  pc_->SetLocalCertificate(kTransportName, local_certinfo->certificate);
+  ASSERT_EQ(local_certinfo->fingerprints.size(), 1u);
+
+  scoped_refptr<const RTCStatsReport> first_report =
+      stats_->GetStatsReport(main_thread_);
+  EXPECT_TRUE(GetCertificateStatsFromFingerprint(
+      first_report, local_certinfo->fingerprints[0]));
+
+  // The handshake completes. No ClearCachedStatsReport(): nothing calls it
+  // when DTLS finishes.
+  std::unique_ptr<CertificateInfo> remote_certinfo =
+      CreateFakeCertificateAndInfoFromDers({"RemoteCertA"});
+  pc_->SetRemoteCertChain(
+      kTransportName,
+      remote_certinfo->certificate->GetSSLCertificateChain().Clone());
+  ASSERT_EQ(remote_certinfo->fingerprints.size(), 1u);
+
+  time_controller_.AdvanceTime(TimeDelta::Seconds(1));
+  scoped_refptr<const RTCStatsReport> second_report =
+      stats_->GetStatsReport(main_thread_);
+  EXPECT_TRUE(GetCertificateStatsFromFingerprint(
+      second_report, local_certinfo->fingerprints[0]));
+  EXPECT_TRUE(GetCertificateStatsFromFingerprint(
+      second_report, remote_certinfo->fingerprints[0]));
+
+  // Complete now, so it is cached: a later remote chain is not picked up
+  // without ClearCachedStatsReport(), exactly as upstream.
+  std::unique_ptr<CertificateInfo> updated_remote_certinfo =
+      CreateFakeCertificateAndInfoFromDers({"UpdatedRemoteCertA"});
+  pc_->SetRemoteCertChain(
+      kTransportName,
+      updated_remote_certinfo->certificate->GetSSLCertificateChain().Clone());
+  time_controller_.AdvanceTime(TimeDelta::Seconds(1));
+  scoped_refptr<const RTCStatsReport> third_report =
+      stats_->GetStatsReport(main_thread_);
+  EXPECT_TRUE(GetCertificateStatsFromFingerprint(
+      third_report, remote_certinfo->fingerprints[0]));
+  EXPECT_FALSE(GetCertificateStatsFromFingerprint(
+      third_report, updated_remote_certinfo->fingerprints[0]));
+}
